## Command

```shell
biome inspect plugins --path=file.js
```

## `biome.json`

```json
{
  "plugins": ["./before.grit"],
  "overrides": [
    {
      "includes": ["**/*.test.js"],
      "plugins": [
        "./missing.grit",
        "./broken",
        {
          "path": "missing-package/presets/recommended",
          "resolutionKind": "project"
        },
        "./after.grit"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

## `after.grit`

```grit
`unterminated
```

## `before.grit`

```grit
`unterminated
```

## `broken/biome-manifest.json`

```json
{ "version": 2 }
```

# Termination Message

```block
configuration ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × 3 plugins in the configuration have errors.
  
  The configuration enables 1 plugin rule for file.js.
  
  Local plugins
  
  - before.grit (rule name: before)
  
  Plugins with errors
  
  missing.grit (override includes: [**/*.test.js])
  
  × Biome couldn't find the plugin file missing.grit.
  
  broken (override includes: [**/*.test.js])
  
  × The Biome manifest broken/biome-manifest.json is invalid.
  
  × Unsupported version 2.
  
  i Biome manifests must use version 1.
  
  missing-package/presets/recommended (override includes: [**/*.test.js])
  
  × Biome couldn't find the plugin package missing-package.
  
  i Make sure the package is installed. Biome looks for it in the node_modules directory of the working directory and of each parent directory.
  
  i Plugins that don't apply to file.js are also reported, because Biome loads every plugin in the configuration.
  


```
